# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/ni-framing.md#on-the-wire
# provenance: PV-0001, PV-0002, PV-0003, PV-0005, PV-0201
# kind: ni-stream
# description: The client's keep-alive answer on the wire: an ordinary frame with length 8 whose payload is NI_PONG\0 (12 bytes in all).
# derivation: u32 BE length 8 (PV-0001, PV-0002, PV-0003), then the 8 literal bytes of PV-0005; PV-0201 states that the answer is framed like the ping; decoding the client's own output must give back one 8-byte frame.
# expect.frames: 1
# expect.frame.1.offset: 4
# expect.frame.1.length: 8
# expect.error: none
# expect.trailing: 0
hex:
00 00 00 08                                       # length 8, u32 BE
4E 49 5F 50 4F 4E 47 00                           # N I _ P O N G \0
